\u3002\u5f00\u53d1\u8005\u65e0\u9700\u4fee\u6539\u4ee3\u7801\u6216\u5de5\u4f5c\u6d41\u3002\n\n4. **Action items for developers**:\n   - \u65e0\u9700\u91c7\u53d6\u4efb\u4f55\u884c\u52a8\u3002\u5982\u679c\u4f60\u5728\u6587\u6863\u6216\u6559\u7a0b\u4e2d\u5f15\u7528\u4e86\u8fd9\u4e9b UI \u63d0\u793a\u6587\u6848\uff0c\u53ef\u540c\u6b65\u66f4\u65b0\u5927\u5c0f\u5199\u4ee5\u4fdd\u6301\u4e00\u81f4\u3002", "reasoning": "Let me analyze these documentation changes:\n\n1. **interactive-mode.md**: Two changes:\n   - `esc` \u2192 `Esc` (capitalization fix for the Escape key)\n   - `continuing automatically` \u2192 `Continuing automatically` (capitalization fix in a conversation message)\n\n2. **vs-code.md**: One change:\n   - Removed the sentence \"Each bar shows how long until its limit resets.\" from the usage bars description.\n\nThese are minor documentation polish changes - capitalization corrections and removal of potentially inaccurate/incomplete information."}, {"timestamp": "15:15 EST", "sources": [{"id": "claude-code", "name": "Claude Code", "pages": [{"slug": "desktop", "source_id": "claude-code", "source_name": "Claude Code", "summary": "+6 lines, -6 lines", "added": 6, "removed": 6, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "devcontainer", "source_id": "claude-code", "source_name": "Claude Code", "summary": "+1 lines, -1 lines", "added": 1, "removed": 1, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "iam", "source_id": "claude-code", "source_name": "Claude Code", "summary": "+9 lines, -2 lines", "added": 9, "removed": 2, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "mcp", "source_id": "claude-code", "source_name": "Claude Code", "summary": "+18 lines, -12 lines", "added": 18, "removed": 12, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "vs-code", "source_id": "claude-code", "source_name": "Claude Code", "summary": "+1 lines", "added": 1, "removed": 0, "analysis": null}]}], "pages": [{"slug": "desktop", "source_id": "claude-code", "source_name": "Claude Code", "summary": "+6 lines, -6 lines", "added": 6, "removed": 6, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "devcontainer", "source_id": "claude-code", "source_name": "Claude Code", "summary": "+1 lines, -1 lines", "added": 1, "removed": 1, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "iam", "source_id": "claude-code", "source_name": "Claude Code", "summary": "+9 lines, -2 lines", "added": 9, "removed": 2, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "mcp", "source_id": "claude-code", "source_name": "Claude Code", "summary": "+18 lines, -12 lines", "added": 18, "removed": 12, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "vs-code", "source_id": "claude-code", "source_name": "Claude Code", "summary": "+1 lines", "added": 1, "removed": 0, "analysis": null}], "analysis": "## \u6279\u91cf\u6587\u6863\u53d8\u66f4\u5206\u6790\n\n### 1. \u603b\u4f53\u6458\u8981\n\n\u672c\u6b21\u66f4\u65b0\u6db5\u76d6 Claude Desktop \u5e03\u5c40\u68c0\u6d4b\u903b\u8f91\u4f18\u5316\u3001OAuth \u767b\u5f55\u6392\u969c\u6307\u5f15\u6539\u8fdb\u3001IAM \u6258\u7ba1\u8bbe\u5907\u65e0\u5bc6\u94a5\u767b\u5f55\u63a7\u5236\u7b56\u7565\u65b0\u589e\u3001MCP \u670d\u52a1\u5668 OAuth \u4ee4\u724c\u64a4\u9500\u4e0e\u5de5\u5177 schema \u5bb9\u9519\u673a\u5236\u589e\u5f3a\uff0c\u4ee5\u53ca VS Code \u6269\u5c55\u65b0\u9519\u8bef\u6d88\u606f\u7684\u8bb0\u5f55\u3002\n\n### 2. \u5173\u952e\u4e3b\u9898\n\n- **\u5e03\u5c40\u68c0\u6d4b\u63cf\u8ff0\u66f4\u7cbe\u786e**\uff1a\u5c06\u6a21\u7cca\u7684\"\u65e0\u73af\u5883\u9009\u62e9\u5668\"\u6539\u4e3a\"\u73af\u5883\u663e\u793a\u5728\u8f93\u5165\u6846\u4e0a\u65b9\u800c\u975e\u4e0b\u65b9\"\uff0c\u5e76\u660e\u786e\u7b2c\u4e09\u65b9\u57fa\u7840\u8bbe\u65bd\u90e8\u7f72\u9700 v4.29.0+ \u624d\u80fd\u4f7f\u7528\u65b0\u5e03\u5c40\n- **OAuth \u767b\u5f55\u6392\u969c\u7edf\u4e00**\uff1adevcontainer \u548c iam \u9875\u9762\u540c\u6b65\u66f4\u65b0\u4e86 OAuth \u767b\u5f55\u5931\u8d25\u7684\u6392\u969c\u6307\u5f15\uff0c\u65b0\u589e\u5bf9 WSL2/SSH/\u5bb9\u5668\u7684\u4ea4\u53c9\u5f15\u7528\n- **\u6258\u7ba1\u8bbe\u5907\u767b\u5f55\u7ba1\u63a7\u6536\u7d27**\uff1a\u65b0\u589e `forceLoginOrgUUID` \u90e8\u7f72\u540e\u7981\u6b62\u65e0\u5bc6\u94a5\u767b\u5f55\u7684\u5b8c\u6574\u7b56\u7565\uff0c\u7ec6\u5316\u4e86\u5404\u7c7b\u51ed\u636e\uff08keyless\u3001\u73af\u5883\u53d8\u91cf\u3001claude.ai\uff09\u7684\u8fc1\u79fb\u5904\u7406\u65b9\u5f0f\n- **MCP OAuth \u4ee4\u724c\u751f\u547d\u5468\u671f\u53d8\u66f4**\uff1a`claude mcp remove` \u4e0d\u518d\u5728\u6388\u6743\u670d\u52a1\u5668\u7aef\u64a4\u9500\u4ee4\u724c\uff0c\u9700\u5148\u6267\u884c `claude mcp logout`\n- **MCP \u5de5\u5177 schema \u5bb9\u9519\u589e\u5f3a**\uff1av2.1.300 \u8d77\uff0c\u5f53 API \u62d2\u7edd\u67d0\u5de5\u5177\u7684 input schema \u65f6\uff0cClaude Code \u6539\u4e3a\u4ee5\u65e0\u53c2\u6570\u5f62\u5f0f\u91cd\u65b0\u53d1\u9001\u8bf7\u6c42\uff08\u800c\u975e\u76f4\u63a5 400 \u62a5\u9519\uff09\uff0c\u5b9e\u73b0\u4f18\u96c5\u964d\u7ea7\n- **MCP \u73af\u5883\u53d8\u91cf\u8fb9\u754c\u884c\u4e3a\u660e\u786e**\uff1a\u7a7a\u5b57\u7b26\u4e32\u89c6\u4e3a\"\u5df2\u8bbe\u7f6e\"\uff0c`${VAR:-default}` \u4e0d\u4f1a\u56de\u9000\u5230 default\n\n### 3. \u5f71\u54cd\u7ea7\u522b\uff1a**Medium**\n\n\u7406\u7531\uff1a\u65e0\u7834\u574f\u6027 API \u53d8\u66f4\uff0c\u4f46\u591a\u9879\u884c\u4e3a\u53d8\u66f4\u4f1a\u5f71\u54cd\u5f00\u53d1\u8005\u65e5\u5e38\u64cd\u4f5c\u2014\u2014MCP \u4ee4\u724c\u64a4\u9500\u6d41\u7a0b\u9700\u624b\u52a8\u8865\u5145\u6b65\u9aa4\u3001\u5de5\u5177 schema \u5bb9\u9519\u884c\u4e3a\u6539\u53d8\u5f71\u54cd\u8c03\u8bd5\u9884\u671f\u3001\u6258\u7ba1\u767b\u5f55\u7b56\u7565\u53d8\u66f4\u5f71\u54cd\u4f01\u4e1a\u90e8\u7f72\u3002\n\n### 4. \u5f00\u53d1\u8005\u884c\u52a8\u9879\n\n- **MCP \u7528\u6237**\uff1a\u5220\u9664\u8fdc\u7a0b\u670d\u52a1\u5668\u524d\u52a1\u5fc5\u5148\u6267\u884c `claude mcp logout <name>`\uff0c\u5426\u5219 OAuth \u4ee4\u724c\u5728\u6388\u6743\u670d\u52a1\u5668\u7aef\u4e0d\u4f1a\u88ab\u64a4\u9500\n- **MCP \u670d\u52a1\u5668\u7ef4\u62a4\u8005**\uff1a\u82e5\u5de5\u5177 schema \u88ab API \u62d2\u7edd\uff0cClaude \u4f1a\u4ee5\u65e0\u53c2\u6570\u5f62\u5f0f\u8c03\u7528\u8be5\u5de5\u5177\uff0c\u9700\u786e\u4fdd\u670d\u52a1\u7aef\u5bf9\u65e0\u53c2\u6570\u8c03\u7528\u6709\u5408\u7406\u7684\u53c2\u6570\u6821\u9a8c/\u9ed8\u8ba4\u503c\u5904\u7406\n- **\u4f01\u4e1a\u7ba1\u7406\u5458**\uff1a\u82e5\u8981\u7981\u6b62\u65e0\u5bc6\u94a5\u767b\u5f55\uff0c\u90e8\u7f72 `forceLoginOrgUUID` \u5230\u6258\u7ba1\u8bbe\u7f6e\u4e2d\uff1b\u4ec5\u8bbe `forceLoginMethod: \"console\"` \u4e0d\u591f\uff0c\u7528\u6237\u4ecd\u53ef\u5728\u91cd\u8bd5\u65f6\u9009\u62e9\u65e0\u5bc6\u94a5\u65b9\u5f0f\n- **\u4f7f\u7528\u73af\u5883\u53d8\u91cf\u9ed8\u8ba4\u503c\u7684 MCP \u914d\u7f6e**\uff1a\u68c0\u67e5\u662f\u5426\u6709\u53d8\u91cf\u88ab\u8bbe\u4e3a\u7a7a\u5b57\u7b26\u4e32\u800c\u975e unset\uff0c\u5426\u5219 `${VAR:-default}` \u4e0d\u4f1a\u5982\u9884\u671f\u56de\u9000\n- **\u7b2c\u4e09\u65b9\u57fa\u7840\u8bbe\u65bd Desktop \u7528\u6237**\uff1a\u786e\u8ba4\u7248\u672c \u2265 v4.29.0 \u4ee5\u83b7\u5f97\u65b0\u5e03\u5c40\u652f\u6301", "reasoning": "Let me analyze the documentation changes across all 5 pages.\n\n1. **desktop.md** - Changes to layout detection and environment selector language. Key changes:\n   - Replaced \"no environment selector\" with \"shows no environment\" or \"shows the environment above the prompt box instead of under it\" - more descriptive language for detecting which layout you have\n   - Updated third-party provider infrastructure layout info: now requires v4.29.0 (was unclear before)\n   - Added \"or repository\" to earlier layout description\n   - Removed a blank line (minor formatting)\n\n2. **devcontainer.md** - Changed the OAuth login troubleshooting note:\n   - Old: advice about copying code when callback doesn't reach container\n   - New: more comprehensive advice covering cases where browser doesn't open OR shows localhost error, directing to use the login URL, and linking to OAuth troubleshooting for WSL2/SSH/containers\n\n3. **iam.md** - Authentication changes:\n   - Removed the note about WSL2/SSH/containers being common for login code issues (simplified)\n   - Changed `forceLoginMethod: \"console\"` behavior: now API key is created without asking only when `forceLoginMethod` is \"console\" AND no `forceLoginOrgUUID` is set, until retry from error screen\n   - New section: \"Stop offering the keyless sign-in on managed machines\" - deploying `forceLoginOrgUUID` prevents keyless sign-in option; detailed guidance on handling credentials when deploying this\n\n4. **mcp.md** - Several changes:\n   - OAuth token revocation: removing a remote server no longer revokes tokens at the authorization server; need to run `claude mcp logout` before `claude mcp remove`\n   - Simplified environment variable expansion docs: merged \"Supported syntax\" and \"Expansion locations\" sections into more concise format\n   - New section on \"Variables set to an empty string\" behavior: empty string counts as set, so `${VAR:-default}` uses empty string, not default\n   - Invalid input schema tools: restructured documentation significantly\n   - New section \"Tools whose input schema the API refuses\": Claude Code now resends request with tool declared without parameters (graceful degradation). Before v2.1.300, it failed with 400 error.\n   - Feature flag fetching behavior clarified more\n\n5. **vs-code.md** - Added a new error message to the troubleshooting table: \"The Claude Code program for this computer, the <build> build, could not be found\"\n\nLet me summarize the themes and impact."}, {"timestamp": "19:48 EST", "sources": [{"id": "claude-code", "name": "Claude Code", "pages": [{"slug": "claude-code-on-the-web", "source_id": "claude-code", "source_name": "Claude Code", "summary": "+3 lines, -2 lines", "added": 3, "removed": 2, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "discover-plugins", "source_id": "claude-code", "source_name": "Claude Code", "summary": "+2 lines, -2 lines", "added": 2, "removed": 2, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "github-actions", "source_id": "claude-code", "source_name": "Claude Code", "summary": "+2 lines, -2 lines", "added": 2, "removed": 2, "analysis